  {
    title: 'File:Ile aux nattes, Madagascar (26043399856).jpg',
    license: 'CC BY-SA 2.0',
    artist: '<a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.flickr.com/people/141297921@N05">krishna naudin</a>',
    description: 'Ile aux nattes, Madagascar'
  },
  {
    title: 'File:Ile-aux-Nattes.jpg',
    license: 'CC BY-SA 3.0',
    artist: '<a href="//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Gloumouth1" title="User:Gloumouth1">Gloumouth1</a>',
    description: 'Île aux Nattes (Nosy Nanto)'
  },
  {
    title: 'File:Unique Madagascar.jpg',
    license: 'CC BY-SA 4.0',
    artist: '<a href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Fabiola_espinoza_castellon&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" class="new" title="User:Fabiola espinoza castellon (page does not exist)">Fabiola espinoza castellon</a>',
    description: 'This picture was taken in Iles aux Nattes, a very small island in the north of Madagascar. At the time this picture was taken, back in 2009, this place was a little piece of heaven in Earth. I remember being waked up by the soothing sound of the waves, to admire the beauty of this land, its crystal water beaches and still conserved nature. I also remember that the inhabitant of this island were beyond gentle and full of aspirations. I remember young girls and boys willing to talk to us, not to receive something, but just by the curiosity of a foreign person in their island. And so, I imagine that by the time I took this picture, this two young boys were caught up in their daily routine, a routine surrounded by peace and the beauty of their island, but I also imagine they had true aspirations for a great future. \n' +
      'More than 10 years later, I hope this island has kept its virgin beauty, and I also hope this boys are living a life they are proud of.'
  }
]
